  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1042 PM MDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nAfter the last several days, dry air finally starts moving in\nbut it'll take a day or two for residual moisture to completely\nleave the area. That means we'll see some convection but it\nshouldn't be as widespread or as strong as what we've seen\nrecently. As the drier air moves in, concerns will shift from\nheavy rain to gusty outflow winds, possibly reaching 50 mph at\ntimes. \n\nHigh pressure then starts to build in over Utah for the weekend\nbringing hot and mostly dry conditions to the region.\nTemperatures will remain hot, reaching about 10 degrees above\nnormal, but with less moisture it'll feel less muggy and more of\na 'dry heat'.",
